[{:db/id 17592186133906 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c3b9fdd0-8dab-5a0b-9e88-9a8e531bca1d" "question-cb3d3dae-b723-59f7-8d1b-568e2e8664df"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c3b9fdd0-8dab-5a0b-9e88-9a8e531bca1d" :question/id #uuid "c3b9fdd0-8dab-5a0b-9e88-9a8e531bca1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-139771" :question/problem "$$\nx={R}^{-1}\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ What is the missing part of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part of the equation is ${Q}^{T}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9cd33a2a-4f98-5342-9ba4-5873365eeaa6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9cd33a2a-4f98-5342-9ba4-5873365eeaa6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9cd33a2a-4f98-5342-9ba4-5873365eeaa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2aaeec0e-9d7d-51b5-8e98-ca8703231590" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b7edffd0-66a0-5c75-bcc7-1841cf561f2f" "answer-e8c7732e-ce78-5352-8708-b204edd3100c" "answer-5a928cee-21d3-53ca-ace1-76f33e1c43e5" "answer-ac5cc7e5-983e-54c2-88c3-dc3f7ef1cb76" "answer-2aaeec0e-9d7d-51b5-8e98-ca8703231590"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7edffd0-66a0-5c75-bcc7-1841cf561f2f" :answer/id #uuid "b7edffd0-66a0-5c75-bcc7-1841cf561f2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(Q-I)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8c7732e-ce78-5352-8708-b204edd3100c" :answer/id #uuid "e8c7732e-ce78-5352-8708-b204edd3100c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a928cee-21d3-53ca-ace1-76f33e1c43e5" :answer/id #uuid "5a928cee-21d3-53ca-ace1-76f33e1c43e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac5cc7e5-983e-54c2-88c3-dc3f7ef1cb76" :answer/id #uuid "ac5cc7e5-983e-54c2-88c3-dc3f7ef1cb76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2aaeec0e-9d7d-51b5-8e98-ca8703231590" :answer/id #uuid "2aaeec0e-9d7d-51b5-8e98-ca8703231590" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Q}^{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cb3d3dae-b723-59f7-8d1b-568e2e8664df" :question/id #uuid "cb3d3dae-b723-59f7-8d1b-568e2e8664df" :question/math-academy-id "q-139772" :question/problem "$$\nx={R}^{-1}{Q}^{T}\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ What is the missing part of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}{Q}^{T}\\,\\,b\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part of the equation is $b.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4202d35-11cb-528d-8f7b-8baa57144892"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4202d35-11cb-528d-8f7b-8baa57144892" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4202d35-11cb-528d-8f7b-8baa57144892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2312d1c9-ae68-5003-ac7e-7414fd467ee9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-425e926e-f6d7-5135-b061-818402d0d1d2" "answer-a8ae5c2d-37b1-5cab-9352-7357b57e7f85" "answer-2312d1c9-ae68-5003-ac7e-7414fd467ee9" "answer-da0250e9-1d30-5606-9e21-317e8cba1e35" "answer-73a71808-3fa5-573e-b8b1-b19de5e75149"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-425e926e-f6d7-5135-b061-818402d0d1d2" :answer/id #uuid "425e926e-f6d7-5135-b061-818402d0d1d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8ae5c2d-37b1-5cab-9352-7357b57e7f85" :answer/id #uuid "a8ae5c2d-37b1-5cab-9352-7357b57e7f85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{b}{‖b‖}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2312d1c9-ae68-5003-ac7e-7414fd467ee9" :answer/id #uuid "2312d1c9-ae68-5003-ac7e-7414fd467ee9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da0250e9-1d30-5606-9e21-317e8cba1e35" :answer/id #uuid "da0250e9-1d30-5606-9e21-317e8cba1e35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73a71808-3fa5-573e-b8b1-b19de5e75149" :answer/id #uuid "73a71808-3fa5-573e-b8b1-b19de5e75149" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{b}^{T}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02febb14-e263-5cc1-8053-2e425b9d6cc5" "question-c07b8d08-df25-5edc-8755-7d7271698aeb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-02febb14-e263-5cc1-8053-2e425b9d6cc5" :question/id #uuid "02febb14-e263-5cc1-8053-2e425b9d6cc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-139783" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ is orthogonal, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4(5) & =-11 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-551c0677-6855-511f-8997-47d81f6ef2d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-551c0677-6855-511f-8997-47d81f6ef2d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "551c0677-6855-511f-8997-47d81f6ef2d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7ccbb9de-1d05-5669-a825-c1565d374612" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39ecad14-1c0a-5aad-bfee-718224c4fd70" "answer-14d72c52-be81-5a78-89ce-5f13fcd20525" "answer-7ccbb9de-1d05-5669-a825-c1565d374612" "answer-d0ba3a48-87bd-5410-a677-49fe3a6248f3" "answer-782b8fc8-baa5-5617-a0d8-b51e87778593"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39ecad14-1c0a-5aad-bfee-718224c4fd70" :answer/id #uuid "39ecad14-1c0a-5aad-bfee-718224c4fd70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14d72c52-be81-5a78-89ce-5f13fcd20525" :answer/id #uuid "14d72c52-be81-5a78-89ce-5f13fcd20525" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ccbb9de-1d05-5669-a825-c1565d374612" :answer/id #uuid "7ccbb9de-1d05-5669-a825-c1565d374612" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0ba3a48-87bd-5410-a677-49fe3a6248f3" :answer/id #uuid "d0ba3a48-87bd-5410-a677-49fe3a6248f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-782b8fc8-baa5-5617-a0d8-b51e87778593" :answer/id #uuid "782b8fc8-baa5-5617-a0d8-b51e87778593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c07b8d08-df25-5edc-8755-7d7271698aeb" :question/id #uuid "c07b8d08-df25-5edc-8755-7d7271698aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-157078" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} & -5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{2} & -5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -10\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}{x}_{1}+2\\sqrt{5}{x}_{2}=-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2}{x}_{2}=-10\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-10.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}{x}_{1}+2\\sqrt{5}(-10) & =-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5}{x}_{1} & =10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c12bf5a-62dd-517a-86dc-485e43650a01"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c12bf5a-62dd-517a-86dc-485e43650a01" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c12bf5a-62dd-517a-86dc-485e43650a01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a7d240b2-f0ec-5826-be4a-8f21e8f0a799" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0a1a00c1-8450-5a4b-9a89-eeb5fc22d5e6" "answer-4c400c42-935c-5527-acc8-5171e1a58778" "answer-a7d240b2-f0ec-5826-be4a-8f21e8f0a799" "answer-3c4ffb51-6024-5d55-874c-2de6b98d1d70" "answer-d1f82732-0e5a-5d26-9566-a09f36539763"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a1a00c1-8450-5a4b-9a89-eeb5fc22d5e6" :answer/id #uuid "0a1a00c1-8450-5a4b-9a89-eeb5fc22d5e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c400c42-935c-5527-acc8-5171e1a58778" :answer/id #uuid "4c400c42-935c-5527-acc8-5171e1a58778" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7d240b2-f0ec-5826-be4a-8f21e8f0a799" :answer/id #uuid "a7d240b2-f0ec-5826-be4a-8f21e8f0a799" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c4ffb51-6024-5d55-874c-2de6b98d1d70" :a