nswer-field-546f4173-148e-5f1a-a1fc-5d267635ba7f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-546f4173-148e-5f1a-a1fc-5d267635ba7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "546f4173-148e-5f1a-a1fc-5d267635ba7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9abe1a9b-a332-59c0-ab49-37957cb6cdaf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7090b097-239e-5212-88fd-47671d2450fe" "answer-ddc48ef6-a7f8-5213-bda3-913460dbb747" "answer-1d0ff9e0-35db-5bc9-91f1-79e039622baa" "answer-cfbebdf1-3a63-5465-be64-fa925058ad05" "answer-9abe1a9b-a332-59c0-ab49-37957cb6cdaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7090b097-239e-5212-88fd-47671d2450fe" :answer/id #uuid "7090b097-239e-5212-88fd-47671d2450fe" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/20/20895cf6185b627cf2081cb9afd248ff1bb3a8b11a988807bfb1a04ada2302f2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddc48ef6-a7f8-5213-bda3-913460dbb747" :answer/id #uuid "ddc48ef6-a7f8-5213-bda3-913460dbb747" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/29/29ab6ef1e10eab020a25bec6c949bebeaf0c2cb5cb77db125f84fd6dd6c88129.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d0ff9e0-35db-5bc9-91f1-79e039622baa" :answer/id #uuid "1d0ff9e0-35db-5bc9-91f1-79e039622baa" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a0/a084209041e41554c744914bf42692c9d6cc77c3d86bb85747c1c62df15aab99.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfbebdf1-3a63-5465-be64-fa925058ad05" :answer/id #uuid "cfbebdf1-3a63-5465-be64-fa925058ad05" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d0/d08c2ac302acf38baa05c091c52a0a1d8fd89570989503f028529e0fa2cd9ff9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9abe1a9b-a332-59c0-ab49-37957cb6cdaf" :answer/id #uuid "9abe1a9b-a332-59c0-ab49-37957cb6cdaf" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/ecb4ff70a833b96a4f0e42ae14e3afff36c5a3fa656fedf45830fe64791db738.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073723 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4afa323a-6ccb-55bc-8693-1338e0d62847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4afa323a-6ccb-55bc-8693-1338e0d62847" :question/id #uuid "4afa323a-6ccb-55bc-8693-1338e0d62847" :question/math-academy-id "q-92138" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4af3047f22d112fd3b1c2689ffacc50a1ce3d53dc458327ba25038f448de9c61.png)\n\nThe model above represents $3$ wholes. Use this model to calculate the value of $3÷\\frac{1}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate $3÷\\frac{1}{7}$, we need to divide each of $3$ wholes into $7$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/19/19b5902c790191dff44c240bb518feeeea9f9ffe5c0c440ca94b59344b78e1eb.png)\n\n \n\nWe get $3\\times 7=21$ pieces in total. \n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{1}{7}=21\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aba16430-0b0e-51ab-956c-4e4440ad03c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aba16430-0b0e-51ab-956c-4e4440ad03c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "aba16430-0b0e-51ab-956c-4e4440ad03c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9cba4bf1-c6c7-5edd-8528-71868f7bbfb1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa4a7e45-1247-5586-a96f-798ff42a6b1a" "answer-4e9be780-5147-51ee-b002-a0f63e5a12b4" "answer-9cba4bf1-c6c7-5edd-8528-71868f7bbfb1" "answer-68111c37-72e6-5fc9-be07-6a3b54ac4ad9" "answer-9ec836ed-be04-5f5e-89ff-824aa2643569"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa4a7e45-1247-5586-a96f-798ff42a6b1a" :answer/id #uuid "fa4a7e45-1247-5586-a96f-798ff42a6b1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e9be780-5147-51ee-b002-a0f63e5a12b4" :answer/id #uuid "4e9be780-5147-51ee-b002-a0f63e5a12b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cba4bf1-c6c7-5edd-8528-71868f7bbfb1" :answer/id #uuid "9cba4bf1-c6c7-5edd-8528-71868f7bbfb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68111c37-72e6-5fc9-be07-6a3b54ac4ad9" :answer/id #uuid "68111c37-72e6-5fc9-be07-6a3b54ac4ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ec836ed-be04-5f5e-89ff-824aa2643569" :answer/id #uuid "9ec836ed-be04-5f5e-89ff-824aa2643569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a2e8b668-df51-5edf-a673-01b58575b2f0" :question/id #uuid "a2e8b668-df51-5edf-a673-01b58575b2f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-137761" :question/problem "![](images/67/675a66c94bee0deba216bf684aa2b74e6fa048ed62a3944dabe50cdbb88952f3.png)\n\nEach of the six shapes in the model above represents one whole. From left to right, what numbers are missing from the division problem below?\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\,\\,}÷\\frac{1}{3}=\\boxed{\\,\\,}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In the model, there are $6$ shapes. Each shape consists of $3$ pieces that each represent $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a whole. There are $18$ pieces in total.\n\nThe model tells us that when we divide $6$ wholes into thirds, we will be left with $18$ pieces.\n\nHence, the division problem is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\,6\\,}÷\\frac{1}{3}=\\boxed{\\,18\\,}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing numbers are $6$ and $18.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-84c38cbc-a594-504c-a843-d261f92675be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-84c38cbc-a594-504c-a843-d261f92675be" :answer-field/id #uuid "84c38cbc-a594-504c-a843-d261f92675be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2d5084db-05d5-56b6-a9d7-ebb87d1f5662" :answer-field/choices ["answer-34761e05-28a7-5780-b0ee-5911ee3484df" "answer-0594fa26-83d8-55d6-ba2f-f5602e974d7e" "answer-2d5084db-05d5-56b6-a9d7-ebb87d1f5662" "answer-bab1da5b-2b3d-5064-9788-38acf0fa6ff8" "answer-e89c2fc3-a3b1-57e9-a10c-59b0f6af795d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34761e05-28a7-5780-b0ee-5911ee3484df" :answer/id #uuid "34761e05-28a7-5780-b0ee-5911ee3484df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ and $18$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0594fa26-83d8-55d6-ba2f-f5602e974d7e" :answer/id #uuid "0594fa26-83d8-55d6-ba2f-f5602e974d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and $12$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d5084db-05d5-56b6-a9d7-ebb87d1f5662" :answer/id #uuid "2d5084db-05d5-56b6-a9d7-ebb87d1f5662" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ and $18$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bab1da5b-2b3d-5064-9788-38acf0fa6ff8" :answer/id #uuid "bab1da5b-2b3d-5064-9788-38acf0fa6ff8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e89c2fc3-a3b1-57e9-a10c-59b0f6af795d" :answer/id #uuid "e89c2fc3-a3b1-57e9-a10c-59b0f6af795d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ and $6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-27bc1257-fd21-5f11-87a5-72c434203efe" :activity/id #uuid "27bc1257-fd21-5f11-87a5-72c434203efe" :activity/title "Dividing Whole Numbers by Unit Fractions Using Models" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050665 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-ac1e36de-ed27-5385-a094-8568c7fcf072" "step-0d938664-32ae-58c2-9276-34c95d3f3781" "step-a126afd0-6b9f-56d3-afce-acd7571f30e0"] :activity/first-step "step-ac1e36de-ed27-5385-a094-8568c7fcf072" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ac1e36de-ed27-5385-a094-8568c7fcf072" :step/id #uuid "ac1e36de-ed27-5385-a094-8568c7fcf072" :step/content "question-a352b711-8af2-5a66-960f-d91f88b29c96" :step/next "step-0d938664-32ae-58c2-9276-34c95d3f3781" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0d938664-32ae-58c2-9276-34c95d3f3781" :step/id #uuid "0d938664-32ae-58c2-9276-34c95d3f3781" :step/content "question-4afa323a-6ccb-55bc-8693-1338e0d62847" :step/next "step-a126afd0-6b9f-56d3-afce-acd7571f30e0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a126afd0-6b9f-56d3-afce-acd7571f30e0" :step/id #uuid "a126afd0-6b9f-56d3-afce-acd7571f30e0" :step/content "question-a2e8b668-df51-5edf-a673-01b58575b2f0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134546 :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $4\\times 3$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The columns of $Q$ are orthogonal\n\nII. $Q$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix\n\nIII. $R$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a  QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are orthogonal.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $Q$ must be a $4\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. $R$ should be a $3\\times 3$ upper triangular matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133314 :answer-field/correct 17592186133315 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133798 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1ccedda5-a7d6-563d-a624-831df95d1f38" "question-ca2de93c-f55b-512e-9e27-ab6ff5bd3cb0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1ccedda5-a7d6-563d-a624-831df95d1f38" :question/id #uuid "1ccedda5-a7d6-563d-a624-831df95d1f38" :question/math-academy-id "q-96039" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained from the columns of $A$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, find  the value of ${q}_{11}\\cdot {r}_{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ be the columns of $A.$\n\nFirst, we find an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**. We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**. We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{24}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & 4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & 4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{12}\\cdot {r}_{22}=(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})\\cdot (4\\sqrt{3})=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-31551476-3b52-57ca-b4de-8bda2f7a95d1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-31551476-3b52-57ca-b4de-8bda2f7a95d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "31551476-3b52-57ca-b4de-8bda2f7a95d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-991358c9-3100-5464-96bd-f2c50332af98" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f86da36a-fea9-5185-a415-54e83a58db6d" "answer-991358c9-3100-5464-96bd-f2c50332af98" "answer-cbd3705e-81e5-5864-b1ab-6314a9b9569b" "answer-c2c797d4-4e44-5a31-83c8-b4dceca7a07d" "answer-9d04ddc7-88d1-5961-b149-0ed80dedcd03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f86da36a-fea9-5185-a415-54e83a58db6d" :answer/id #uuid "f86da36a-fea9-5185-a415-54e83a58db6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-991358c9-3100-5464-96bd-f2c50332af98" :answer/id #uuid "991358c9-3100-5464-96bd-f2c50332af98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbd3705e-81e5-5864-b1ab-6314a9b9569b" :answer/id #uuid "cbd3705e-81e5-5864-b1ab-6314a9b9569b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2c797d4-4e44-5a31-83c8-b4dceca7a07d" :answer/id #uuid "c2c797d4-4e44-5a31-83c8-b4dceca7a07d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d04ddc7-88d1-5961-b149-0ed80dedcd03" :answer/id #uuid "9d04ddc7-88d1-5961-b149-0ed80dedcd03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca2de93c-f55b-512e-9e27-ab6ff5bd3cb0" :question/id #uuid "ca2de93c-f55b-512e-9e27-ab6ff5bd3cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96041" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained from the columns of $A$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, find  the value of ${q}_{22}\\cdot {r}_{22}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ be the columns of $A.$\n\nFirst, we find an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**. We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**. We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{6}{12}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & 0\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{22}\\cdot {r}_{22}=(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})\\cdot (2\\sqrt{2})=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-36df5534-c619-54f6-902b-ac3c15f3e762"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36df5534-c619-54f6-902b-ac3c15f3e762" :answer-field/id #uuid "36df5534-c619-54f6-902b-ac3c15f3e762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9557cf45-32ca-5990-b9e7-8944ea966b53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7cce974d-ff76-5e44-b28b-aec2865278ff" "answer-072eda89-f2fd-5e6b-8865-e919b2deb069" "answer-9557cf45-32ca-5990-b9e7-8944ea966b53" "answer-a3b55a48-54cb-5cad-b04e-d24581a88559" "answer-6acfb0da-27b6-5749-b6e8-62595ebc8056"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cce974d-ff76-5e44-b28b-aec2865278ff" :answer/id #uuid "7cce974d-ff76-5e44-b28b-aec2865278ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-072eda89-f2fd-5e6b-8865-e919b2deb069" :answer/id #uuid "072eda89-f2fd-5e6b-8865-e919b2deb069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9557cf45-32ca-5990-b9e7-8944ea966b53" :answer/id #uuid "9557cf45-32ca-5990-b9e7-8944ea966b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3b55a48-54cb-5cad-b04e-d24581a88559" :answer/id #uuid "a3b55a48-54cb-5cad-b04e-d24581a88559" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6acfb0da-27b6-5749-b6e8-62595ebc8056" :answer/id #uuid "6acfb0da-27b6-5749-b6e8-62595ebc8056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f03b2cb7-71f2-5a0a-b8dc-a0edc6ff3419" :activity/id #uuid "f03b2cb7-71f2-5a0a-b8dc-a0edc6ff3419" :activity/title "QR Factorization" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050130 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-cd1623be-2e54-562c-8cfd-19ef37f01b2e" "step-558490e4-84ba-51db-b8e6-e71608372b63" "step-f89604cd-9e6c-5431-9cc6-02eee87bc460" "step-ba9899ad-e46c-5454-a574-beabe6f5c8c7" "step-8870d163-7037-5417-a28f-0af8d578e0cb"] :activity/first-step "step-cd1623be-2e54-562c-8cfd-19ef37f01b2e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-cd1623be-2e54-562c-8cfd-19ef37f01b2e" :step/id #uuid "cd1623be-2e54-562c-8cfd-19ef37f01b2e" :step/content 17592186134546 :step/next "step-558490e4-84ba-51db-b8e6-e71608372b63" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-558490e4-84ba-51db-b8e6-e71608372b63" :step/id #uuid "558490e4-84ba-51db-b8e6-e71608372b63" :step/content 17592186364599 :step/next "step-f89604cd-9e6c-5431-9cc6-02eee87bc460" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f89604cd-9e6c-5431-9cc6-02eee87bc460" :step/id #uuid "f89604cd-9e6c-5431-9cc6-02eee87bc460" :step/content "question-1ccedda5-a7d6-563d-a624-831df95d1f38" :step/next "step-ba9899ad-e46c-5454-a574-beabe6f5c8c7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ba9899ad-e46c-5454-a574-beabe6f5c8c7" :step/id #uuid "ba9899ad-e46c-5454-a574-beabe6f5c8c7" :step/content "question-ca2de93c-f55b-512e-9e27-ab6ff5bd3cb0" :step/next "step-8870d163-7037-5417-a28f-0af8d578e0cb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8870d163-7037-5417-a28f-0af8d578e0cb" :step/id #uuid "8870d163-7037-5417-a28f-0af8d578e0cb" :step/content 17592186363231 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068791 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cabf388f-9bb5-5253-94f0-ab94c951c5d3" "question-0bef42fa-eb7d-5919-88c0-11096c328a79" "question-f364a39c-30aa-5ef8-a564-e4bf60255f6e" "question-a13b920e-64ea-55ab-8027-087f421742e4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068428 :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $-1,$ the value of $f(x)$ approaches $2.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,-1}f(x)=2\\,.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068533 :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $0,$ the value of $f(x)$ approaches $1.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,0}f(x)= 1\\,.\n$$\n\nRemember, it does not matter that the actual value of $f(0)$ is $2.$ All that matters is that as $x$ approaches $0,$ the function $f(x)$ *looks like* it is getting closer and closer to $1$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068534 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true concerning the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is shown below? \n\nI. $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,0}f(x)=0$\n\nII. $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,3}f(x)=0$\n\nIII. $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,-1}f(x)=\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,1}f(x)$\n\n![](images/68/68241f3cd913cd91d10765499dc4ce4398fb3e8a81ec4bcfb65b47c0d77731d6.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As $x$ approaches $0,$ the function $f(x)$ approaches the value $y=-1.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,0}f(x)=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. As $x$ approaches $3,$ the function $f(x)$ approaches the value $y=0.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,3}f(x)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ approaches $-1$ the function $f(x)$ approaches the value $y=2,$ and consequently\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,-1}f(x)=2.\n$$\n\nSimiliarly, as $x$ approaches $1,$ the function $f(x)$ approaches the value $y=-2,$ and consequently\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,1}f(x)=-2.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,-1}f(x)\\ne\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\,1}f(x).\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-cabf388f-9bb5-5253-94f0-ab94c951c5d3" :question/id #uuid "cabf388f-9bb5-5253-94f0-ab94c951c5d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105924" :question/problem "![](images/83/83919380982c0c572d248f6de55122bbcb8529fc48d16a3ff1b1e1865754bef1.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ for the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above." :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $-1,$ the value of $f(x)$ approaches $-3.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)=-3\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-591ccfce-b1eb-567e-a446-303b602da094"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-591ccfce-b1eb-567e-a446-303b602da094" :answer-field/id #uuid "591ccfce-b1eb-567e-a446-303b602da094" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a970a39e-bf7b-525b-a111-50b3b263c304" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ced337f3-f977-5d08-9438-9cb5cc025cc6" "answer-a970a39e-bf7b-525b-a111-50b3b263c304" "answer-d27606be-2d6d-58cf-b41e-b69f5c34405f" "answer-e5d9aac2-bbad-553e-966e-262d594be4f1" "answer-e7152016-6a94-5546-8bb4-6639e2c74869"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ced337f3-f977-5d08-9438-9c