:question/math-academy-id "q-118283" :question/problem "![](images/39/392fab62a445326d26f7c637735cb03f13d94139ec0141d1802c8617020b1489.png)\n\nConsider the vector $a,$ shown above. Which of the following could be $a+(-a)?$" :question/worked-solution "According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $-a.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain a new vector for which the tail and head is the same point, the tail of $a.$ \n\nThat vector is called the zero vector, and we write\n\n$$\na+(-a)=0.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/96/96172072cf76df18a675eb506207756e65b7458e2f3c5fa056f54a81335fc6de.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-760e2ee6-413b-5589-acb9-b8d03aa02863"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-760e2ee6-413b-5589-acb9-b8d03aa02863" :answer-field/id #uuid "760e2ee6-413b-5589-acb9-b8d03aa02863" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a23b7a2-f1f6-520e-ad41-1ab5c9c5c23b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4804b665-6cb2-5324-a8a3-a7b1dd1bf48a" "answer-1a23b7a2-f1f6-520e-ad41-1ab5c9c5c23b" "answer-574b2518-c168-5aa4-a98f-c7376cd2c3f4" "answer-56cd32a0-fad3-576e-9ba0-52fba4bd4ded" "answer-70d220ae-db4e-58c0-bc4a-b01f0765dde4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4804b665-6cb2-5324-a8a3-a7b1dd1bf48a" :answer/id #uuid "4804b665-6cb2-5324-a8a3-a7b1dd1bf48a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/bb/bb1554a6e02728076dbaf90e02aba2f87f6bfa33309a7da9060740da92b5fcf3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a23b7a2-f1f6-520e-ad41-1ab5c9c5c23b" :answer/id #uuid "1a23b7a2-f1f6-520e-ad41-1ab5c9c5c23b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cf/cfcee1a944e477bd909ef749d8d5d8967176340c359c664f0a97c887db5ab82d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-574b2518-c168-5aa4-a98f-c7376cd2c3f4" :answer/id #uuid "574b2518-c168-5aa4-a98f-c7376cd2c3f4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d3/d366405b4fd522a8edaf6e2cf82eb7b97e6dc6869439b8035e55b6631ba4dced.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56cd32a0-fad3-576e-9ba0-52fba4bd4ded" :answer/id #uuid "56cd32a0-fad3-576e-9ba0-52fba4bd4ded" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ed/ed5b0908aee7c2a2fbf065087ff2b09df5294b83c986e2d325489aba2eee3459.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70d220ae-db4e-58c0-bc4a-b01f0765dde4" :answer/id #uuid "70d220ae-db4e-58c0-bc4a-b01f0765dde4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f0/f0ed0a1903d642e78d103d17a3fb309af76c6f792c3a9244b3c24607f165899f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-78aa3546-9c22-5075-a931-7cce83bce972" :question/id #uuid "78aa3546-9c22-5075-a931-7cce83bce972" :question/math-academy-id "q-118277" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f05b638b28790b3bc87bc8e76b10092fdd13dde6d4c3dc98b93c7e92401f28fc.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above. Which of the following could be $-a?$" :question/worked-solution "The vector $-a$ has the same magnitude as $a$ but goes in the direction opposite to $a$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c5/c5fb5b587a0e0f72cd73a7439420d153562dffec79f15e9dfa46e5167ac85196.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d9c88a4e-4ffc-5aa5-af97-379732d75b6c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d9c88a4e-4ffc-5aa5-af97-379732d75b6c" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9c88a4e-4ffc-5aa5-af97-379732d75b6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd7938ed-c187-5415-b99b-a7e07ab8de2d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06edd154-245c-5e62-964d-008ce8a8084b" "answer-a87aa98e-0dfc-5bae-b156-f7898c0b5266" "answer-93cec5d4-cb50-5639-802a-c80bf37e3c9c" "answer-bd7938ed-c187-5415-b99b-a7e07ab8de2d" "answer-e019953e-8155-5c35-ad70-6d7c34ecb858"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06edd154-245c-5e62-964d-008ce8a8084b" :answer/id #uuid "06edd154-245c-5e62-964d-008ce8a8084b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/56/564070d6b3db6d074045156b005b091ddcb55adca401f00256f6810995903863.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a87aa98e-0dfc-5bae-b156-f7898c0b5266" :answer/id #uuid "a87aa98e-0dfc-5bae-b156-f7898c0b5266" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/65/65be75c62725c429579265b81d0c79686013c795cd3281e667c95d25feef3d64.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93cec5d4-cb50-5639-802a-c80bf37e3c9c" :answer/id #uuid "93cec5d4-cb50-5639-802a-c80bf37e3c9c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/90/90fe2ee6c4141f34a17ad7d22b9488893c544a4d998a9c4f2e704427e574c5da.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd7938ed-c187-5415-b99b-a7e07ab8de2d" :answer/id #uuid "bd7938ed-c187-5415-b99b-a7e07ab8de2d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f4/f469bc9939f4c9224a9f7a7b00698d6fb61f9798b6b09be985d1a6da2149022c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e019953e-8155-5c35-ad70-6d7c34ecb858" :answer/id #uuid "e019953e-8155-5c35-ad70-6d7c34ecb858" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fb/fb502cf1d7e5c6698f067f04b84483c69c628308048600815447688b51669e19.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d8718b0-c85d-5066-80fb-cb2a1380aab6" :question/id #uuid "6d8718b0-c85d-5066-80fb-cb2a1380aab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-118289" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb7d3c1f1cf1ed19c22bad9eefc9f8c4911d70ed74231c5d63ed88a6cd710a67.png)\n\nThe diagram shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$  Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector subtraction $-a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "We interpret  $-a+b$ as the addition\n\n$$\n(-a)+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $-a$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $a$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $a.$\n\nFinally, we use the triangle law to add the vectors $-a$ and $b:$ \n\n- We can start $-a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane.\n\n- Next, we draw the vector that is equal to $b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $-a.$\n\n- Now, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $-\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c21de8788e5808a48d725252c6308e817b756ca20cc6bbe0446fbfc124440c58.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a2c501f0-31c4-5fe0-aad9-a91029b26492"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a2c501f0-31c4-5fe0-aad9-a91029b26492" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2c501f0-31c4-5fe0-aad9-a91029b26492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-742051e9-131c-51fe-a81d-a856798f59c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61b62ed2-e6fa-508e-be46-05972095da9e" "answer-742051e9-131c-51fe-a81d-a856798f59c4" "answer-7f187e8d-d99b-5d1e-af89-9dce1640528d" "answer-536b7056-cf83-5b72-abab-db8c3a002129" "answer-5ef4d82a-905f-5ae8-9b37-4644e9232ab2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61b62ed2-e6fa-508e-be46-05972095da9e" :answer/id #uuid "61b62ed2-e6fa-508e-be46-05972095da9e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/2a/2a25a65f2ec4cc43a53051f739b999a55e807c509bc74c97852c837ea09a33db.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-742051e9-131c-51fe-a81d-a856798f59c4" :answer/id #uuid "742051e9-131c-51fe-a81d-a856798f59c4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9a/9a5dc1c9f479702ef746df13ca445b3fea68e0452e36e51ddff2622a19f24a84.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f187e8d-d99b-5d1e-af89-9dce1640528d" :answer/id #uuid "7f187e8d-d99b-5d1e-af89-9dce1640528d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b6/b660479554e1f8f9a7106e0bc949eac8a97cd06ac676479ec38ef119f454973d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-536b7056-cf83-5b72-abab-db8c3a002129" :answer/id #uuid "536b7056-cf83-5b72-abab-db8c3a002129" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/dc/dceca1f109a6377db0877e6ccb1c0e950a3288cc7953757884f6ea16e9c21467.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ef4d82a-905f-5ae8-9b37-4644e9232ab2" :answer/id #uuid "5ef4d82a-905f-5ae8-9b37-4644e9232ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f2/f26c0030cd9d17197218ceb6d639edc5ff85ae93c20624ad67f66eefc1ff9e8c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a6578d74-834c-5f37-879c-4ad4b226d0f1" :question/id #uuid "a6578d74-834c-5f37-879c-4ad4b226d0f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-118284" :question/problem "![](images/98/98619223439f3dbbb12f7849bfdb787ef952245569c16e7edf59b07ef908abd0.png)\n\nThe diagram shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$  Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector subtraction $a-b.$" :question/worked-solution "We interpret the subtraction\n$a-b$\nas the addition\n\n$$\na+(-b),\n$$\n\nwhere $-b$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $b$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $b.$\n\nFinally, we use the triangle law to add the vectors $a$ and $-b:$ \n\n- We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane.\n\n- Next, we draw the vector that is equal to $-b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $a.$\n\n- Now, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $-\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/09/0990751c1d413600cba164bd50b732742b73ccc8bc0bcf3a3c039bc3693d8d5f.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-af40cf27-ae86-54b2-948f-89455e9c5039"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af40cf27-ae86-54b2-948f-89455e9c5039" :answer-field/id #uuid "af40cf27-ae86-54b2-948f-89455e9c5039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fdf72d52-c34d-592d-91cc-ff5e4833cdbc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdf72d52-c34d-592d-91cc-ff5e4833cdbc" "answer-a53d4220-b392-5cd3-80ab-9ad8d6ddf03f" "answer-32cf3ae7-e0ab-587b-b543-788e926bdf9a" "answer-b13f7bba-eb3e-5e0c-bbc0-77b62c492c1a" "answer-4a337005-76c4-5a52-8411-24dfc17a2ff2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdf72d52-c34d-592d-91cc-ff5e4833cdbc" :answer/id #uuid "fdf72d52-c34d-592d-91cc-ff5e4833cdbc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/08/08adcd569189cfa3ecc99ab4bc6f7ecde7fb1f0b9bb4be54978865a4dfc972b4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a53d4220-b392-5cd3-80ab-9ad8d6ddf03f" :answer/id #uuid "a53d4220-b392-5cd3-80ab-9ad8d6ddf03f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/56/56120a02f93b94c08baa445f22b34ef290165ce02609f25eb50e52a472c0db24.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32cf3ae7-e0ab-587b-b543-788e926bdf9a" :answer/id #uuid "32cf3ae7-e0ab-587b-b543-788e926bdf9a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a5/a504ce78e5701a958f4a787bb1d2ed3a3d324027c992f8549085b68910216946.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b13f7bba-eb3e-5e0c-bbc0-77b62c492c1a" :answer/id #uuid "b13f7bba-eb3e-5e0c-bbc0-77b62c492c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f5/f55985250120af1277bc64d7e9b25215ae16b1a3cbffb21f98647b5617788c4c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a337005-76c4-5a52-8411-24dfc17a2ff2" :answer/id #uuid "4a337005-76c4-5a52-8411-24dfc17a2ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f9/f9ea26f5540fbd4d5486bcd0e3cb810b167b160b4f612a51b781b8433d5573b0.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d8517d92-ae69-5efd-a845-0b2600987e0b" :question/id #uuid "d8517d92-ae69-5efd-a845-0b2600987e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-69482" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f1af14d60c9b2353d3aa149c4f74ead097289fd2a619013f1506cb783b72ee2.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{a},$ $\\text{b},$ and $\\text{c}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\na-b=a+(-b).\n$$\n\nThe resultant $a-b$ is the vector that joins the tail of $\\text{a}$ and the head of $-\\text{b}:$\n\n![](images/40/40912329e0fa213a0bb8be143ed2d44441634ced3eaf378d76a69aa3167fe14c.png)\n\nNow, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\n(\\text{a}-\\text{b})-\\text{c}=(\\text{a}-\\text{b})+(-\\text{c}).\n$$\n\nWe draw $-\\text{c}$ from the head of $\\text{a}-\\text{b}.$ So, we have the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $-\\text{c}:$\n\n![](images/6c/6cbd0e043e9de98da0044792d5be99df0e1a17eff3b9dc8b87093985c5a27f24.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-025afa14-11d3-50a3-94aa-2f8842d9174c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-025afa14-11d3-50a3-94aa-2f8842d9174c" :answer-field/id #uuid "025afa14-11d3-50a3-94aa-2f8842d9174c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0bf8e4cf-c0f3-551b-abbb-fb80164ac96f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35b2ecbb-8412-549e-8ee4-b7b2ac3428dd" "answer-326c84ac-e8aa-52e0-9dc1-13238a3daa00" "answer-320b3562-cbad-56db-a302-8849208fccef" "answer-2064542d-12af-569c-b701-32bc6eb0c259" "answer-0bf8e4cf-c0f3-551b-abbb-fb80164ac96f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35b2ecbb-8412-549e-8ee4-b7b2ac3428dd" :answer/id #uuid "35b2ecbb-8412-549e-8ee4-b7b2ac3428dd" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/47/478de116b8b2364cc324046da2a102e1ff159d99bdfdd517ed26d75864bd6d33.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-326c84ac-e8aa-52e0-9dc1-13238a3daa00" :answer/id #uuid "326c84ac-e8aa-52e0-9dc1-13238a3daa00" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/4e/4e131814caab231af9390de4443f281bea8179fd07b61a08b8931062a735a1ca.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-320b3562-cbad-56db-a302-8849208fccef" :answer/id #uuid "320b3562-cbad-56db-a302-8849208fccef" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/59/597d3779c6748c4c96b9b43e30751f8443031091bb015048cc56a3fa8d04cf6f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2064542d-12af-569c-b701-32bc6eb0c259" :answer/id #uuid "2064542d-12af-569c-b701-32bc6eb0c259" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/95/955d3bed564303d79a3047310df139fce20ad698cc45c0c353f53608f2c1e57c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bf8e4cf-c0f3-551b-abbb-fb80164ac96f" :answer/id #uuid "0bf8e4cf-c0f3-551b-abbb-fb80164ac96f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/da/da52e611ffe7002e478024073ec134e4f5b6a6d1b12f19513fed24a0b03ba25b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aa07fa75-e006-5c8d-9bd3-e38658b1ba33" :question/id #uuid "aa07fa75-e006-5c8d-9bd3-e38658b1ba33" :question/math-academy-id "q-118546" :question/problem "![](images/92/926161e90964be4d6d4d32491ce4b6fdfa7e964d5d88ebc4eb7dd367dd2a837f.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{a},$ $\\text{b},$ and $\\text{c}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $a-b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\na-b=a+(-b).\n$$\n\nThe resultant $a-b$ is the vector that joins the tail of $\\text{a}$ and the head of $-\\text{b}:$\n\n![](images/a4/a487c6406c591962ce27be6c27006c2d8f2ef49d05ee704007d578788db77883.png)\n\nNow, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\n(\\text{a}-\\text{b})+\\text{c}.\n$$\n\nWe draw $\\text{c}$ from the head of $\\text{a}-\\text{b}.$ So, we have the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{c}:$\n\n![](images/12/122df7ad9d20a94049597c1a75adf75f8286b7e67ca9b9a661029e21fea6393c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ffad1de5-4c55-5caf-87c3-832fe971927a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ffad1de5-4c55-5caf-87c3-832fe971927a" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffad1de5-4c55-5caf-87c3-832fe971927a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-665a5698-611b-5436-bcea-96432be92280" :answer-field/choices ["answer-665a5698-611b-5436-bcea-96432be92280" "answer-8c7dd4b9-2650-576f-ab1b-cd43c6a18f9c" "answer-2292cb83-da06-5374-8569-708024b1dd67" "answer-7a1f03d1-fdc7-5f23-9f51-0b77b3e898bd" "answer-3f699177-2c7e-5534-8699-7c3f00a58bdf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-665a5698-611b-5436-bcea-96432be92280" :answer/id #uuid "665a5698-611b-5436-bcea-96432be92280" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/12/122df7ad9d20a94049597c1a75adf75f8286b7e67ca9b9a661029e21fea6393c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c7dd4b9-2650-576f-ab1b-cd43c6a18f9c" :answer/id #uuid "8c7dd4b9-2650-576f-ab1b-cd43c6a18f9c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/17/17cf4643da768e10a7c71107d5092d4a8ff3eb9628782765571bd3ab9fe2de16.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2292cb83-da06-5374-8569-708024b1dd67" :answer/id #uuid "2292cb83-da06-5374-8569-708024b1dd67" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/28/28fc327298fb61bcd4140abb1c74bd4749efe0c339cf411afe4b99ce4c07400c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a1f03d1-fdc7-5f23-9f51-0b77b3e898bd" :answer/id #uuid "7a1f03d1-fdc7-5f23-9f51-0b77b3e898bd" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9d/9dba0cd378e980b7f6935a8db01aa1e4338630926146df217e7e17d282fd39d4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f699177-2c7e-5534-8699-7c3f00a58bdf" :answer/id #uuid "3f699177-2c7e-5534-8699-7c3f00a58bdf" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d8/d82556efc5965f68de5d68663ab6a60d7dac94a3d1b49b9cd8ee306fad38f105.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097828 :tutorial/content "Given two vectors, we can compute the sum by placing the head of one vector at the tail of the other.\n\nFor example, let's consider the two vectors $\\textbf{a}$ and $\\textbf{b}$ below.\n\n![](images/04/049f79ae22e5931a7ceba7f73fef5cb6bc38d17c2a45e7186d57f8760b02488a.png)\n\nTo find $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b},$ we need to draw the second vector $\\textbf{b}$ starting from the head of the first vector $\\textbf{a}.$ Now, the sum $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ is the vector that we get when we join the tail of $\\textbf{a}$ to the head of $\\textbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/98/98a42bc3ecf7071630acc7d29349f75f77b20a9cc1c2c34382161cc79b47b4df.png)\n\nWe call this method the **triangle law of addition**. The vector obtained by adding two or more vectors is sometimes called the **resultant**." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097830 :tutorial/content "Given a vector $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ the **opposite vector** is the vector $\\overrightarrow{BA}$ that has the same length but goes in the opposite direction.\n\n![](images/65/6591fd004ba2b74c2651182ce0c70302ac789d868389d057a502b8e98ac61fab.png)\n\nWe write\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AB}=-\\overrightarrow{BA}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the sum of two opposite vectors,\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AB}+\\overrightarrow{BA},\n$$\n\nwe can use the triangle law of addition.\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ to the head of $\\overrightarrow{BA}.$ Therefore, we obtain a new vector for which the tail and head are the same point, $A.$ We denote that vector as\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AB}+\\overrightarrow{BA} = \\overrightarrow{AA}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nThe vector $\\mathbf{0}$ is called the **zero vector**. The zero vector has no direction and zero magnitude. With the zero vector, the head coincides with the tail." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097838 :tutorial/content "We've seen how to use the triangle law to add two vectors. We can also use the triangle law to subtract two vectors.\n\nThe trick is to interpret the subtraction as the addition of a negative vector. For example, the subtraction\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\ncan be interpreted as the addition\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} + (-\\mathbf{b}),\n$$\n\nwhere $-\\mathbf{b}$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $\\mathbf{b}$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nLet's see a concrete example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096880 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221418 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-59916f2b-317a-58b9-929b-11913732d3cd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-59916f2b-317a-58b9-929b-11913732d3cd" :question/id #uuid "59916f2b-317a-58b9-929b-11913732d3cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-335133" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+{y}^{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)-5y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations above. What is the corresponding linearized system at the equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}=[0,\\text{ }0]^{T}?$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${u}^{′}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"50px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"50px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,u,\\,$ where $u=x-{x}^{∗}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The system can be rewritten in matrix form as \n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x)=[\\begin{aligned}4x+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-5y\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe need to compute the Jacobian matrix (or the total derivative) of $\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x+{y}^{2})=4,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x+{y}^{2})=2y \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-5y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-5y)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2y \\\\ 2x & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2(0) \\\\ 2(0) & -5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, near the equilibrium, the nonlinear system is approximated by\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]u,\n$$\n\nwhere the deviation vector is\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f24f971e-0879-530e-bc3b-f3a08731a8aa" "answer-field-b9b52cf4-5cc3-561a-bfeb-9f02941ae255" "answer-field-a1006ef8-7090-5491-a5a2-d9fd36d5275f" "answer-field-3fb562b6-3ffd-5817-bd9b-9192877cbc82"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f24f971e-0879-530e-bc3b-f3a08731a8aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "f24f971e-0879-530e-bc3b-f3a08731a8aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6cd4ad32-eeac-5002-877f-b890f2b10896" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cd4ad32-eeac-5002-877f-b890f2b10896"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cd4ad32-eeac-5002-877f-b890f2b10896" :answer/id #uuid "6cd4ad32-eeac-5002-877f-b890f2b10896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9b52cf4-5cc3-561a-bfeb-9f02941ae255" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b52cf4-5cc3-561a-bfeb-9f02941ae255" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-216ca193-a489-5830-9a58-4e49ef86790a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-216ca193-a489-5830-9a58-4e49ef86790a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-216ca193-a489-5830-9a58-4e49ef86790a" :answer/id #uuid "216ca193-a489-5830-9a58-4e49ef86790a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1006ef8-7090-5491-a5a2-d9fd36d5275f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1006ef8-7090-5491-a5a2-d9fd36d5275f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8397406b-3741-58c6-be48-cb822d70a432" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8397406b-3741-58c6-be48-cb822d70a432"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8397406b-3741-58c6-be48-cb822d70a432" :answer/id #uuid "8397406b-3741-58c6-be48-cb822d70a432" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3fb562b6-3ffd-5817-bd9b-9192877cbc82" :answer-field/id #uuid "3fb562b6-3ffd-5817-bd9b-9192877cbc82" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c5a55fdf-f65f-595c-83d0-6e0cb10b7741" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5a55fdf-f65f-595c-83d0-6e0cb10b7741"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5a55fdf-f65f-595c-83d0-6e0cb10b7741" :answer/id #uuid "c5a55fdf-f65f-595c-83d0-6e0cb10b7741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221419 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83d63d6d-d88e-5a5d-adf3-8972165ae385"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83d63d6d-d88e-5a5d-adf3-8972165ae385" :question/id #uuid "83d63d6d-d88e-5a5d-adf3-8972165ae385" :question/math-academy-id "q-336954" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=xy-{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations above. What is the behavior of the system’s solutions near the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}={[2,\\text{ }1]}^{T}?$\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium is an  \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The system can be rewritten in matrix form as \n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $x=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x)=[\\begin{aligned}xy-{y}^{2}-1 \\\\ -{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe need to compute the Jacobian matrix (or the total derivative) of $\\text{\\boldsymbol}f(x).$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-{y}^{2}-1)=y \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{y}^{2}-1)=x-2y \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+5)=-2x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+5)=-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y & x-2y \\\\ -2x & -2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}(1) & 2-2(1) \\\\ -2(2) & -2(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), so the system is almost linear at ${x}^{∗}.$\n\nTo find the eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix, we write down the characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation, we get the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=-2,1.$\n\nFinally, since we have two real eigenvalues with opposite signs, our equilibrium is an $\\text{unstable}$ $\\text{saddle}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c715942c-d2c2-5b4c-ae37-5167cb54c7d2" "answer-field-b50e47a7-1678-588a-bc35-ad270c59097b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c715942c-d2c2-5b4c-ae37-5167cb54c7d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c715942c-d2c2-5b4c-ae37-5167cb54c7d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f054de3f-c85f-5fce-886d-2896608021dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c1ef6b60-5a30-5b50-bc9b-fd1b1fc59d06" "answer-f054de3f-c85f-5fce-886d-2896608021dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1ef6b60-5a30-5b50-bc9b-fd1b1fc59d06" :answer/id #uuid "c1ef6b60-5a30-5b50-bc9b-fd1b1fc59d06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "asymptotically stable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f054de3f-c85f-5fce-886d-2896608021dc" :answer/id #uuid "f054de3f-c85f-5fce-886d-2896608021dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "unstable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b50e47a7-1678-588a-bc35-ad270c59097b" :answer-field/id #uuid "b50e47a7-1678-588a-bc35-ad270c59097b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-866d6d61-ec02-5461-a9af-e13501b74bec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-866d6d61-ec02-5461-a9af-e13501b74bec" "answer-e8d35f3f-1137-54b9-bd30-758c448db7b0" "answer-34ade299-a613-5a23-987e-23a091542225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-866d6d61-ec02-5461-a9af-e13501b74bec" :answer/id #uuid "866d6d61-ec02-5461-a9af-e13501b74bec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "saddle" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8d35f3f-1137-54b9-bd30-758c448db7b0" :answer/id #uuid "e8d35f3f-1137-54b9-bd30-758c448db7b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "spiral sink" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34ade299-a613-5a23-987e-23a091542225" :answer/id #uuid "34ade299-a613-5a23-987e-23a091542225" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "spiral source" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c7291f65-7a36-5e3f-9242-7648b94cd8a9" :activity/id #uuid "c7291f65-7a36-5e3f-9242-7648b94cd8a9" :activity/title "Linear Approximations Near Equilibria" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048881 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-2cb4bb92-6182-5d82-adf8-726f3c1f7eaa" "step-70dd2bb3-126f-59ed-855a-f46120b28c5e" "step-819b91a6-5d0d-5137-8403-162591cc718d" "step-372bc3a9-4bde-54ec-8f9c-e9a568ca29f6" "step-ecc8f232-f4d0-52b1-8514-442214380c29"] :activity/first-step "step-2cb4bb92-6182-5d82-adf8-726f3c1f7eaa" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2cb4bb92-6182-5d82-adf8-726f3c1f7eaa" :step/id #uuid "2cb4bb92-6182-5d82-adf8-726f3c1f7eaa" :step/content 17592186368143 :step/next "step-70dd2bb3-126f-59ed-855a-f46120b28c5e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-70dd2bb3-126f-59ed-855a-f46120b28c5e" :step/id #uuid "70dd2bb3-126f-59ed-855a-f46120b28c5e" :step/content "question-59916f2b-317a-58b9-929b-11913732d3cd" :step/next "step-819b91a6-5d0d-5137-8403-162591cc718d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-819b91a6-5d0d-5137-8403-162591cc718d" :step/id #uuid "819b91a6-5d0d-5137-8403-162591cc718d" :step/content 17592186368175 :step/next "step-372bc3a9-4bde-54ec-8f9c-e9a568ca29f6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-372bc3a9-4bde-54ec-8f9c-e9a568ca29f6" :step/id #uuid "372bc3a9-4bde-54ec-8f9c-e9a568ca29f6" :step/content "question-83d63d6d-d88e-5a5d-adf3-8972165ae385" :step/next "step-ecc8f232-f4d0-52b1-8514-442214380c29" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ecc8f232-f4d0-52b1-8514-442214380c29" :step/id #uuid "ecc8f232-f4d0-52b1-8514-442214380c29" :step/content 17592186368201 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186193179 :question/answer-fields 17592186190960] {:db/id 17592186193179 :question/problem "![](images/b9/b95c538613ee8672e0f1cac970b7af230ec40bf3075e609b1e03f7cad4382fb1.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/19/19e8e52881066864cba562ed2a8cdc2944b9dae416c7124fdee207cdad1d8bdf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/90/907e996fb7aea36e0c924feb0f5d9dc6804c768be775953d277e84b0145ef5a0.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,-1<y<0\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378843 :question/problem "![](images/80/80bde6a20ceed7c052a87eda6f05c542f6046de7014f6402f5f453b6610f8d42.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05b25521109f373e2a7718523ce6289b27b37bd185d4fc60f0d052c232f4f8a4.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=-1+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=-1+x\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281310 :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa335a55f5b4496cdaccca5d35e286a168598761188bc520c81397ef136f927d.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/fb/fba9ba3e52ed19eb0bb2286ae59c49bb9dc648134d9eab3c4e2d13862963f736.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f3cd30dbaa4f84c43f2a7f1197aa904e3d43b1212241ae26736b2a0087f6170.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3da69255-8e25-5787-aeff-55f176c9e5f1" :activity/id #uuid "3da69255-8e25-5787-aeff-55f176c9e5f1" :activity/title "Interiors and Boundaries of Sets" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048621 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-ad2d8f33-f769-5b19-b3a8-2c1054e52764" "step-3aeb6357-d3cb-58b4-a333-6689b626b0b1" "step-b46780df-21b0-590b-bec2-f3671aa2cd9f" "step-b277a6a0-e989-50db-857a-8b156c750f75" "step-c5efa418-7310-57f8-a775-d17dbd515940"] :activity/first-step "step-ad2d8f33-f769-5b19-b3a8-2c1054e52764" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ad2d8f33-f769-5b19-b3a8-2c1054e52764" :step/id #uuid "ad2d8f33-f769-5b19-b3a8-2c1054e52764" :step/content 17592186193179 :step/next "step-3aeb6357-d3cb-58b4-a333-6689b626b0b1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3aeb6357-d3cb-58b4-a333-6689b626b0b1" :step/id #uuid "3aeb6357-d3cb-58b4-a333-6689b626b0b1" :step/content 17592186193206 :step/next "step-b46780df-21b0-590b-bec2-f3671aa2cd9f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b46780df-21b0-590b-bec2-f3671aa2cd9f" :step/id #uuid "b46780df-21b0-590b-bec2-f3671aa2cd9f" :step/content 17592186378843 :step/next "step-b277a6a0-e989-50db-857a-8b156c750f75" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b277a6a0-e989-50db-857a-8b156c750f75" :step/id #uuid "b277a6a0-e989-50db-857a-8b156c750f75" :step/content 17592186278575 :step/next "step-c5efa418-7310-57f8-a775-d17dbd515940" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c5efa418-7310-57f8-a775-d17dbd515940" :step/id #uuid "c5efa418-7310-57f8-a775-d17dbd515940" :step/content 17592186281310 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
